WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar, reminding you to "Mind Your Decisions".

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.120
Here's a fun problem I found online.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.060
This unusual shape has three right angles as marked.

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:16.379
Also, its side lengths are four, three, four, and five.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:24.449
The question is: What is the value of the last side's length (which is marked as 'x' in the diagram)?

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:31.740
Pause if you'd like to give it a try, and when you're ready keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:44.240
[Music]

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.940
So I'll briefly mention, the solution I'm going to present

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:54.420
is very similar to another video where you had to solve for x, the length of this square's side.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.049
We're going to use a little "outside-the-box" thinking.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.570
So in our diagram,

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:05.159
the first thing I'm going to do is I'm going to draw it a little bit to scale.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.300
This will just help in our presentation.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.520
Now let's connect these two points,

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.879
we're going to figure out this distance,

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.580
but how can we do that?

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:21.540
Well, let's focus just on these three sides.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:27.980
Now let's rotate them, so it'll be a little easier to understand the distance between the two endpoints

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:35.670
I'm going to join the "3" side with the "5" side and then I'm going to bring the "4" side to the left.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:43.469
We have a right triangle where 1 leg is 4 and the other leg is 3+5 which equals 8.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:50.249
We can solve for its hypotenuse as the square root of the sum of the squares of its sides.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.909
This will be the square root of 4 squared plus 8 squared.

00:01:54.939 --> 00:01:57.449
So now let's go back to our original diagram.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.359
So we know this is the same distance from endpoint to endpoint,

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.680
and we're going to bring it back to our unusual shape.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:11.369
And now, let's just focus on this right triangle.

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:15.269
What is the value of x in this right triangle?

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:21.560
Well, we know that the length of the hypotenuse will be the square root of 4 squared plus x squared

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:29.340
and it's also equal to the square root of 4 squared plus 8 squared. Therefore x is equal to 8 and that's our answer!

00:02:29.859 --> 00:02:35.459
I know there are other ways to solve this problem, but I thought this one was very fun, and I wanted to share it with you.

00:02:36.609 --> 00:02:41.219
Thanks for watching and for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:47.760
Thanks for watching and thanks for your support.

